 "researcher_notes": "Not a match to an existing row: the only related row is P0281, the whole Williston Basin system (3364 mi), which has no segment for this project. This is a stand-alone 60.2 mile expansion, so it is a new row in the expansion shape (parent system name, project as segment). The operator project page states 60.2 miles of 12-inch pipe from the Mapleton Compressor Station to a new delivery station near Wahpeton, North Dakota, also serving Kindred, and says it was placed in service December 1, 2024 after a FERC certificate on October 23, 2023. The EIA release dated Aug 2026 (sheet Historical Projects, Excel row 1123) lists it as Completed, 60 miles, 12 inch, 20.6 MMcf/d added, 75 million dollars, FERC docket CP22-466. EIA pages and operator page are independent of the FERC and MDU Resources notices, which also fit (FERC final environmental impact statement and certificate approval); the FERC and MDU pages sit behind a bot check and loaded only through the verifier fallback. Value of 20,600 Dth/d in the FERC statement is consistent with EIA 20.6 MMcf/d. Status operating and start year 2024 from the operator page. No official route data found, so route is staged as unavailable. Owner WBI Energy and parent MDU Resources Group Inc match existing gazetteer entries. Passes the length rule (60.2 mi is about 97 km of new pipe)."
